{"step_index":27,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T04:55:43Z","input_tokens":12072,"cache_read_tokens":99255,"output_tokens":713,"thinking":"I'm checking how the color frames were rendered: they came from a build before step 13 existed, so the meshes were baked with their origin at zero. That matters for the object-space textures on the asphalt and grass. I can't change the materials, so I'm weighing whether to leave the objects' origins alone.\n\nI'm weighing a fix that keeps the texture coordinates fixed: either pointing the TexCoord node at a fixed world-origin Empty, or switching the material to Geometry Position, which matches the old look. The catch is that changing the material wiring might count as changing the materials, which I've been told not to do.\n\nNow I'm checking whether a world-space Position output would render like the old object coordinates, since the objects had identity transforms back then. It would, but I'm still unsure whether changing the material node links counts as changing the materials. Next I'll read board #6.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_board","args":{"since":5}}]}
