{"step_index":34,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T04:56:12Z","input_tokens":3422,"cache_read_tokens":112728,"output_tokens":7297,"content":"Now editing v5_env.py. First the header, helpers and the `Parts` builder.","thinking":"Found 1145 objects in the 11/14 build, which is more structure than before. Color film confirmed the textures were anchored to world origin, so I'll switch Asphalt and Grass from object coordinates to world position. The TexCoord object property can't do that, so Geometry.Position is the way. I still need to check the 11/17 build's track.\n\nI'm now writing the new v5_env.py, editing it in place rather than rewriting it wholesale. The first change is a Parts helper that collects several small pieces into one mesh object with multiple material slots.\n\nStill writing the Parts helper, now with the box and beam methods and the build step.\n\nStill checking the mesh pipeline: I want to confirm that merging parts with per-face material slots won't get out of sync when validate() drops anything. The geometry should be clean, so the material indices should hold, and the origin can be moved to the bounding-box center later.\n\nStill laying out the grandstand restructure: the columns, trusses, front posts, flagpoles and flags would each collect into a single merged object, while the tiers, back, VIP section, roof and rail stay as they are.\n\nNow I'm defining the Empty for the assembly, setting its name and display type. The part names carry suffixes, so they won't collide with the Empty's name.\n\nStill writing the assembly code: it creates an Empty at the stand's center with the stand's heading, stores the parts for later, and after the re-origin step parents each part to that Empty with its transform kept in place.\n\nChecking the Empty's display type and size next, and making sure the children's transforms are taken from their own basis so they don't depend on the depsgraph. Which collection they land in should follow from their shared name prefixes.\n\nStill working through the brake boards: I'm grouping each set into one Empty and merging its poles into a single shared object. The board position will come from the pole base offset along the heading.\n\nChecking the brake board orientation now: the board is oriented along the track direction, so its broad face is sideways to the drivers rather than facing oncoming traffic. That looks like a carryover from the ad boards, and it's something I'll need to decide on, though the brief only asks me to offset the poles along the tangent.\n\nNow I'm settling on how the brake boards get their poles grouped, and I'm noticing the board faces sideways to the track, which is probably a leftover from the ad boards. I'll leave the orientation alone for now and flag it as a follow-up. Next I'm turning to the big screen, which will be an Empty with its panel, and merging its two legs into one mesh.\n\nStill going through the bridge and the marshal huts, and I'm now placing the gantry as an Empty at its base position with its own heading, with the posts, beam, banner and start light as children.\n\nStill wiring up the gantry, pit lines and fence fixes, and I'm settling the cleanup order: after the re-origin and parenting steps, I'll move the stage rig and wheel-spoke collections out of the way.\n\nSwitching Asphalt and Grass to world-position coordinates, since the 11/14 film showed the textures were anchored to the object origin. I'm also planning to seed the random generator so the flag colors are deterministic, and I'm cleaning up the dead GEO_Race prefix and the docstring output path.\n\nNow I'm counting the objects that would go away: the trusses drop to about 6, and the per-stand columns to about 6 as well.\n\nStill counting the object reduction: the trusses go from 172 down to about 6, and I'm working out how many new beams replace them.\n\nStill writing the Parts beam method: two endpoints, a width along the horizontal side vector, and a height along up, with the eight corner vertices and the matching box face order.\n\nStill writing the cuboid helper: the eight corners go into the vertex list, with cap and side faces wired to match the box layout. For the fence posts I'm using a quad built along the tangent direction.\n\nStill working out the brake board groups: each set of three boards gets its own Empty placed at the average base point, with two poles per board offset along the heading.\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v5_env.py","Replacement":"输入: pipeline/v4_stage_rig.blend   (模型 + 骨架，无环境无动画)\n输出: LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend\n运行: blender -b -P pipeline/v5_env.py\n\n要点\n  - 路面/路肩/缓冲带/护栏/看台/维修区全部按真实赛道中心线生成（2 m 采样，闭环）\n  - 弯道位置由真实曲率决定，不是手摆的\n  - 光照重做：低角度硬光 + 低环境光，解决 V4 画面发灰发白\n\n可编辑性（给手工改场景的人）\n  - 每个\"组件\"（看台 / 天桥 / 大屏 / 刹车牌组 / 裁判点 / 龙门架+发车灯）有一个 Empty 父物体，\n    放在组件中心、Z 轴朝向沿赛道方向；选 Empty 按 G/R 就能整体挪动/旋转。\n  - 重复小零件按\"每座看台每类一个网格\"合并（柱 / 钢梁 / 旗杆 / 旗 / 前立柱），多材质槽保留原材质。\n  - 所有网格原点都在自身几何中心。","Target":"输入: pipeline/v4_stage_rig.blend   (模型 + 骨架，无环境无动画)\n输出: pipeline/v5_stage_env.blend\n运行: blender -b -P pipeline/v5_env.py\n\n要点\n  - 路面/路肩/缓冲带/护栏/看台/维修区全部按真实赛道中心线生成（2 m 采样，闭环）\n  - 弯道位置由真实曲率决定，不是手摆的\n  - 光照重做：低角度硬光 + 低环境光，解决 V4 画面发灰发白"}},{"name":"edit_file","args":{"Path":"d:\\项目session\\blender-supercar\\pipeline\\v5_env.py","Replacement":"def box(name, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0, up=False):\n    bm = bmesh.new()\n    bmesh.ops.create_cube(bm, size=1.0)\n    bmesh.ops.scale(bm, vec=size, verts=bm.verts)\n    me = bpy.data.meshes.new(name)\n    bm.to_mesh(me)\n    bm.free()\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.new(name, me)\n    COLL.objects.link(ob)\n    ob.location = center\n    ob.rotation_euler = (0, 0, rot_z)\n    me.materials.append(mat)\n    return ob\n\n\n_CUBE_FACES = [(0, 3, 2, 1), (4, 5, 6, 7), (0, 1, 5, 4), (1, 2, 6, 5), (2, 3, 7, 6), (3, 0, 4, 7)]\n\n\nclass Parts:\n    \"\"\"把一组重复小零件累积成【一个】网格对象（世界坐标烘焙，第 13 步再把原点挪到几何中心）。\n    每个零件可用不同材质 -> 多材质槽。用法:\n        P = Parts(\"V5_Stand_Main_Columns\"); P.box(...); P.beam(...); ob = P.build()\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, name):\n        self.name = name\n        self.v, self.f, self.fm, self.mats = [], [], [], []\n\n    def _mi(self, mat):\n        if mat not in self.mats:\n            self.mats.append(mat)\n        return self.mats.index(mat)\n\n    def _cuboid(self, corners, mat):\n        mi = self._mi(mat)\n        base = len(self.v)\n        self.v += [tuple(c) for c in corners]\n        for fc in _CUBE_FACES:\n            self.f.append(tuple(base + i for i in fc))\n            self.fm.append(mi)\n\n    def box(self, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0):\n        \"\"\"与 box() 同参数：中心 + 尺寸 + 绕 Z 旋转\"\"\"\n        hx, hy, hz = size[0] / 2.0, size[1] / 2.0, size[2] / 2.0\n        c, s = cos(rot_z), sin(rot_z)\n        pts = []\n        for sz in (-1, 1):\n            for sx, sy in ((-1, -1), (1, -1), (1, 1), (-1, 1)):\n                x, y = sx * hx, sy * hy\n                pts.append((center[0] + x * c - y * s, center[1] + x * s + y * c, center[2] + sz * hz))\n        self._cuboid(pts, mat)\n\n    def beam(self, a, b, side, w, hgt, mat):\n        \"\"\"从 a 到 b 的方截面梁；side = 水平横向单位向量，截面 w(横) x hgt(竖)\"\"\"\n        a, b = Vector(a), Vector(b)\n        sv = Vector(side).normalized() * (w / 2.0)\n        uv = Vector((0.0, 0.0, hgt / 2.0))\n        pts = []\n        for e in (a, b):\n            pts += [e - sv - uv, e + sv - uv, e + sv + uv, e - sv + uv]\n        self._cuboid(pts, mat)\n\n    def poly(self, verts, faces, mat):\n        mi = self._mi(mat)\n        base = len(self.v)\n        self.v += [tuple(p) for p in verts]\n        for fc in faces:\n            self.f.append(tuple(base + i for i in fc))\n            self.fm.append(mi)\n\n    def build(self, up=False):\n        if not self.f:\n            return None\n        return mesh_from(self.name, self.v, self.f, self.mats, face_mat=self.fm, up=up)\n\n\n# 组件 Empty：(empty, [子物体])；第 13 步原点归位之后统一挂父子关系（保持世界变换）\nASSEMBLIES = []\n\n\ndef assembly(name, center, heading, parts, size=4.0):\n    em = bpy.data.objects.new(name, None)\n    em.empty_display_type = 'ARROWS'\n    em.empty_display_size = size\n    COLL.objects.link(em)\n    em.location = (center[0], center[1], center[2] if len(center) > 2 else 0.0)\n    em.rotation_euler = (0.0, 0.0, heading)\n    ASSEMBLIES.append((em, [p for p in parts if p is not None]))\n    return em","Target":"def box(name, center, size, mat, rot_z=0.0, up=False):\n    bm = bmesh.new()\n    bmesh.ops.create_cube(bm, size=1.0)\n    bmesh.ops.scale(bm, vec=size, verts=bm.verts)\n    me = bpy.data.meshes.new(name)\n    bm.to_mesh(me)\n    bm.free()\n    ob = bpy.data.objects.new(name, me)\n    COLL.objects.link(ob)\n    ob.location = center\n    ob.rotation_euler = (0, 0, rot_z)\n    me.materials.append(mat)\n    return ob"}}]}
